    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Migrate libmirisdr to the maintained upstream fork f4exb/libmirisdr-4 and
update from the 2013 osmocom snapshot 0.0.0+git.20130608 to release 2.0.0.

Supersedes SR 1373844, which declared the mirisdr-udev subpackage as
GPL-3.0-or-later. That subpackage now inherits the package-wide
GPL-2.0-or-later; see the licence note below. Nothing else changed.

The osmocom libmirisdr repository the package tracked has seen no commit
since June 2013. Debian, Ubuntu, Kali, OpenMandriva, Raspbian and ROSA all
ship the f4exb fork; Debian carries the same 2.0.0 release.

SONAME / REBUILD SCOPE - please note for staging:

  The fork bumped the SONAME from libmirisdr.so.0 to libmirisdr.so.4, so
  the shared library subpackage libmirisdr0 is renamed to libmirisdr4.
  libmirisdr4 carries Provides: libmirisdr0 = %{version}-%{release} and
  Obsoletes: libmirisdr0 &lt; %{version}-%{release} so installed systems
  upgrade cleanly, and libmirisdr-devel now requires libmirisdr4.

  Three packages in Factory pull libmirisdr in:

    gr-osmosdr  - uses the API. Rebuilt locally on aarch64 against the new
                  library: build succeeded, rpmlint unchanged from its
                  Factory baseline, and libgnuradio-osmosdr now requires
                  libmirisdr.so.4()(64bit).
    soapy-osmo  - uses the API. Rebuilt locally on aarch64 against the new
                  library: build succeeded, rpmlint clean, and the
                  soapysdr module now requires libmirisdr.so.4()(64bit).
    gqrx        - does not link libmirisdr at all; it only requires
                  libgnuradio-osmosdr.so.0.2.0 and reaches libmirisdr
                  transitively through gr-osmosdr. No source change needed.

  The public API is a strict superset of the 2013 snapshot: every entry
  point the old header declared is still present with an unchanged
  signature, which is why both API consumers build unmodified.

Other packaging changes:

  - Source is now the upstream release tarball; the _service and
    _servicedata files that tracked the dormant osmocom git repository
    are dropped, and URL points at the fork.
  - libmirisdr-cmake-libsuffix.diff dropped: the fork already applies the
    library suffix to the pkg-config file and to its install location.
  - libmirisdr-release-version.patch added: upstream leaves the patch
    level at &quot;git&quot; in its release archives, which yields an empty
    pkg-config version and a library named libmirisdr.so.4.0git. The
    patch declares the patch level so the release builds
    libmirisdr.so.4.0.0 behind SONAME libmirisdr.so.4. Debian carries the
    equivalent change. It is a distro patch and is not going upstream.
  - License corrected from the deprecated GPL-2.0 to GPL-2.0-or-later,
    uniformly across every subpackage, which is what the headers of every
    compiled source file grant and what COPYING contains. Two files carry
    a GPL-3.0-or-later header instead: the shipped udev rules file, and
    the CMake build system, which is not shipped in any binary package.
    Both are recorded in a Legal-Review-Notice above the License tag so
    the finding does not have to be re-derived, rather than split out
    into a separate subpackage tag - the same way other distributions
    declare this package.
  - The new miri_fm FM demodulator is packaged next to miri_sdr.
  - mirisdr-udev is now noarch and its udev_rules_update scriptlets are
    dropped, they are a no-op now that udev ships a file trigger.
  - Spec cleanup: %cmake_build, %license, %ldconfig_scriptlets, explicit
    shared library file names, Group tags and %defattr removed, git-core
    build requirement dropped, -DCMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RPATH=ON because
    upstream hardcodes an install RPATH of /usr/lib.

Built locally on aarch64 against openSUSE_Tumbleweed: succeeded, rpmlint
0 errors / 1 warning / 0 badness, down from 1 error / 1 warning / 1
badness (mirisdr-udev no-binary, gone now that it is noarch). Upstream
ships no test suite, hence no %check.</comment>
    <requestid>1373863</requestid>
